 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s1": "Overview",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s2": "A full profile of this artist's inscriptions",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s3": "Works by period",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s4": "Sentiment shifts across life stages",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s5": "If the late-period shift is far below the early one, life circumstances strongly shaped the artist's emotional register. Higher weight means the period influences the overall analysis more.",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s6": "Sentiment Analysis",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s7": "A panoramic scan of the paintings' moods",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s8": "Sentiment polarity distribution",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s9": "Mood timeline",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s10": "The outliers in the scatter plot deserve a click — there hide the artist's most honest moments.",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s11": "Theme Analysis",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s12": "What the artist said in inscriptions",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s13": "Themes by period",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s14": "For artists with a high share of self-reflection, inscriptions are first-hand material for understanding their worldview — truer than any biography.",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s15": "Inscription Style",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s16": "Quantitative patterns of length and area",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s17": "Inscription length by period",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s18": "Works where inscription length suddenly grows often mark the artist's most emotionally charged periods — there hide the words they most wanted to say.",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s19": "Seals & Dimensions",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s20": "Sentiment contribution of six dimensions",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s21": "Engine dimension radar",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s22": "Seals are stamped deliberately by the artist — the most \"honest\" emotional signal, unlike inscriptions that can be revised over and over.",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s23": "Sentiment Ranking",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s24": "The most emotionally extreme works — click for details",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s25": "Most Negative Top 10",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s26": "Most Positive Top 10",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s27": "Compare the two columns — the wider the emotional range, the richer and more complex the artist's inner world.",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s28": "Space & Form",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s29": "Painting size and inscription strategy",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s30": "Painting size vs inscription share",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s31": "Layout statistics",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s32": "Artists who favor interleaved layouts show spatial innovation — they treat inscriptions as part of the painting, not an appendix.",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s33": "Materials & Sizes",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s34": "What was painted, and on how large a sheet",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s35": "Material tag statistics",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s36": "Work size distribution",
 "artist.artistanalysisslides.s37": "When a flower-and-bird painter suddenly turns to \"withered trees\" and \"lotus in decay\" in late years, it often signals a change of heart — subjects are the artist's ECG.",
